---
/**
 * Fig. 1 — how EHR data reaches the two applications, and where access control sits.
 * The claim: adapters come from a shared base module, so a new hospital source is closer
 * to configuration than integration; RBAC at the last hop lets one backend serve both
 * audiences without leaking between them.
 */
---

<figure>
  <div class="figbox">
    <svg
      viewBox="0 0 920 250"
      role="img"
      style="min-width:620px"
      aria-label="Hospital EHR systems are read by per-source adapters built from a shared base module, which publish to a Pub/Sub topic. Backend services subscribe asynchronously with dead-letter handling, and a role-based access layer filters responses before they reach the study team app and the participant app."
    >
      <defs>
        <marker id="tp-ar" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
          <path d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z" fill="currentColor"></path>
        </marker>
        <marker id="tp-hl" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
          <path class="hlfill" d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z"></path>
        </marker>
      </defs>

      <g font-size="12" fill="currentColor">
        <rect x="8" y="86" width="118" height="58" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2"></rect>
        <text x="67" y="110" text-anchor="middle">Hospital</text>
        <text x="67" y="127" text-anchor="middle">EHR</text>

        <rect x="186" y="86" width="118" height="58" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2"></rect>
        <text x="245" y="110" text-anchor="middle">Adapter</text>
        <text x="245" y="127" text-anchor="middle" opacity="0.62">shared base</text>

        <rect x="364" y="86" width="118" height="58" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2"></rect>
        <text x="423" y="110" text-anchor="middle">Pub/Sub</text>
        <text x="423" y="127" text-anchor="middle" opacity="0.62">topic</text>

        <rect x="542" y="86" width="118" height="58" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2"></rect>
        <text x="601" y="110" text-anchor="middle">Backend</text>
        <text x="601" y="127" text-anchor="middle" opacity="0.62">services</text>

        <rect class="hl" x="716" y="76" width="58" height="78" fill="none" stroke-width="1.6"></rect>
        <text class="hl" x="745" y="107" text-anchor="middle">RBAC</text>
        <text class="hl" x="745" y="124" text-anchor="middle" opacity="0.75">gate</text>

        <rect x="812" y="50" width="100" height="46" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2"></rect>
        <text x="862" y="70" text-anchor="middle">Study team</text>
        <text x="862" y="86" text-anchor="middle">app</text>

        <rect x="812" y="146" width="100" height="46" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2"></rect>
        <text x="862" y="166" text-anchor="middle">Participant</text>
        <text x="862" y="182" text-anchor="middle">app</text>

        <line x1="126" y1="115" x2="180" y2="115" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" marker-end="url(#tp-ar)"></line>
        <text x="153" y="76" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" opacity="0.72">FHIR</text>

        <line x1="304" y1="115" x2="358" y2="115" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" marker-end="url(#tp-ar)"></line>
        <text x="331" y="76" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" opacity="0.72">publishes</text>

        <line x1="482" y1="115" x2="536" y2="115" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" marker-end="url(#tp-ar)"></line>
        <text x="509" y="76" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" opacity="0.72">subscribes</text>
        <text x="509" y="164" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" opacity="0.55">async + DLQ</text>

        <line x1="660" y1="115" x2="710" y2="115" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" marker-end="url(#tp-ar)"></line>

        <line class="hl" x1="774" y1="103" x2="806" y2="78" stroke-width="1.4" marker-end="url(#tp-hl)"></line>
        <line class="hl" x1="774" y1="127" x2="806" y2="164" stroke-width="1.4" marker-end="url(#tp-hl)"></line>
        <!-- sits in the clear gap between the two app boxes (y 96–146), so it cannot
             collide with the RBAC box on its left -->
        <text class="hl" x="862" y="126" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5" opacity="0.85">filtered by role</text>
      </g>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    <b>Fig. 1 — Every hospital connection follows one shape.</b>
    Adapters are generated from a shared base module rather than written from scratch, so a
    new EHR source is closer to a configuration problem than a new integration. Access
    control sits at the last hop, which is how one backend serves both the clinical staff
    view and the participant view without leaking between them.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
